---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Books — The Antariksha Protocol"
  description="Hard science fiction novels by Prasad Ajinkya exploring cis-lunar geopolitics, vacuum engineering, and human survival in deep space."
>
  <main>
    <div class="books-hero">
      <span class="books-hero-eyebrow">Hard Science Fiction &bull; ISRO-Punk</span>
      <h1>The Antariksha Protocol</h1>
      <p>
        An epic space exploration and survival saga grounded in the philosophy of frugal, high-efficiency engineering (&ldquo;ISRO-punk&rdquo;), cis-lunar resource geopolitics, and deep-space anomaly retrieval. In the killing dark of 2068, humanity&rsquo;s first war in space isn&rsquo;t fought for glory&mdash;it is fought for water, air, and sovereignty.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Featured: Book 1 -->
    <article class="book-card featured">
      <div class="book-cover-wrap">
        <img
          src="/images/books/the-shackleton-ice-rush.jpg"
          alt="The Shackleton Ice Rush book cover"
          class="book-cover-img"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>

      <div class="book-content">
        <div class="book-header">
          <span class="book-series-tag">Book 1 &bull; The Antariksha Protocol</span>
          <h2 class="book-title">The Shackleton Ice Rush</h2>
          <div class="book-subtitle">A Hard Science Fiction Novel of Cis-Lunar Geopolitics</div>
          <div class="book-badges">
            <span class="book-badge available">&check; Available Now</span>
            <span class="book-badge">Hard Sci-Fi</span>
            <span class="book-badge">Space Survival</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="book-blurb">
          <p>
            <strong>On the Moon, water is life. And someone is willing to choke the entire colony to own it.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            At the lunar South Pole, technician <strong>Karan &ldquo;KT&rdquo; Tiwari</strong> harvests ancient water-ice trapped in the permanent shadows of Shackleton Crater. When a blowout ruptures Sublimation Conduit 4B, KT unearths something impossible: an exotic non-terrestrial metallic lattice that absorbs radar and pulses with an unnatural frequency.
          </p>
          <p>
            Two million kilometers away in the Asteroid Belt, salvage captain <strong>Revathi Sundaram</strong> harpoons an uncharted asteroid ringing with the exact same signal. When corporate syndicates trigger an enforced blackout to seize the discoveries, technicians on the rim and defiant flight directors in Bengaluru must pull off a desperate orbital gamble before Chandragiri Station suffocates.
          </p>

          <div class="book-quote">
            &ldquo;In space, water is not merely a beverage; it is air to breathe, hydrogen to burn, and dense mass to shield human cells from cosmic radiation. In space, water is Amrit&mdash;the currency of the future.&rdquo;
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="book-actions">
          <div class="book-action-label">Get the Book on Amazon:</div>
          <a
            href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJP2TVSH"
            class="btn-amazon btn-amazon-primary"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Amazon US &bull; Kindle
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJNSGV6L"
            class="btn-amazon btn-amazon-primary"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Amazon US &bull; Paperback
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://www.amazon.in/dp/B0HJP2TVSH"
            class="btn-amazon btn-amazon-secondary"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Amazon India &bull; Kindle
          </a>
          <a
            href="https://www.amazon.in/dp/B0HJNSGV6L"
            class="btn-amazon btn-amazon-secondary"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >
            Amazon India &bull; Paperback
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <!-- Upcoming Books & Spinoffs -->
    <div class="books-section-title">The Saga Continues &bull; Upcoming Releases</div>

    <div class="books-grid-secondary">
      <!-- Book 2 -->
      <article class="book-card-mini">
        <div class="book-cover-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/books/the-iron-monsoon.jpg"
            alt="The Iron Monsoon book cover"
            class="book-cover-img"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="book-header">
          <span class="book-series-tag">Book 2</span>
          <h3 class="book-title">The Iron Monsoon</h3>
          <div class="book-badges">
            <span class="book-badge upcoming">In Production</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="book-blurb">
          <p>
            A coronal shockwave tears across cis-lunar space, turning orbits into radioactive furnaces. As syndicates weaponize water reserves, labor organizer Zoya Khan calls the greatest zero-g strike in history while KT blueprints the <em>Indra-Kavach</em>&mdash;a 14-Tesla magnetic storm shield built from scrap railway superconductors.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Book 3 -->
      <article class="book-card-mini">
        <div class="book-cover-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/books/the-antariksha-sovereign.jpg"
            alt="The Antariksha Sovereign book cover"
            class="book-cover-img"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="book-header">
          <span class="book-series-tag">Book 3</span>
          <h3 class="book-title">The Antariksha Sovereign</h3>
          <div class="book-badges">
            <span class="book-badge upcoming">In Production</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="book-blurb">
          <p>
            A 12,000-year magnetic inversion detonates within the sun, unleashing a 100-billion-ton coronal tsunami. Humanity has ninety days before the wave incinerates Earth's power grid. Defying fleeing oligarchs, off-world outcasts forge the <em>Maha-Kavach</em> planetary shield anchored to Asteroid 3140-Shiva.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>

      <!-- Companion Novella -->
      <article class="book-card-mini">
        <div class="book-cover-wrap">
          <img
            src="/images/books/the-gravity-between-us.jpg"
            alt="The Gravity Between Us book cover"
            class="book-cover-img"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <div class="book-header">
          <span class="book-series-tag">Companion Novella</span>
          <h3 class="book-title">The Gravity Between Us</h3>
          <div class="book-badges">
            <span class="book-badge companion">Bengaluru 2068</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="book-blurb">
          <p>
            Set concurrent with <em>The Shackleton Ice Rush</em>. In torrential 2068 Bengaluru, an ISRO flight dynamics specialist and a cynical AI systems engineer clash over non-linear gravity equations, filter coffee, and corporate espionage in a sci-tech romance.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
